# Production AWS frontend env template — DO NOT USE YET

This file is **not** loaded by Vite. It is the source of truth for an operator
production AWS SPA build (`vite build --mode aws` with these values copied
privately). Do **not** copy this over `.env.production`.

- Do **not** point it at the **staging** Cognito pool (`us-east-1_vPmQ7cL1F`) or staging API.
- Do **not** put RDS passwords, AWS keys, or provider secrets in any `VITE_*` variable.
- Production provider execution stays disabled on the API (`AWS_PROVIDER_EXECUTION_ENABLED=false`).
- Step 2 API URL is **same-origin `/prep`**, not the raw execute-api hostname.
  `awsApiBaseUrl()` resolves `/prep` against `window.location.origin` so
  `www.checksops.com` stays same-origin. Do **not** hardcode `https://checksops.com/prep`.
- Raw execute-api remains the Step 1–2 rollback URL and must stay enabled.

Production `.env.production` remains the repo Supabase-only file.

```
# Uncomment only on an approved Step 2 production AWS frontend deploy.
# VITE_AUTH_PROVIDER=cognito
# VITE_APP_URL=https://checksops.com
# Same-origin CloudFront API (apex and www):
# VITE_CHECKSOPS_API_URL=/prep
# Step 2 rollback (do not ship after Step 2):
# VITE_CHECKSOPS_API_URL=https://kiqojucc02.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/prep
# VITE_AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=us-east-1_h00WorYMT
# VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_CLIENT_ID=3ja9fqaq2fjkv3i6up2varcqpe
# CloudFront domain: https://dmgs35lzv89ms.cloudfront.net
# Do not set VITE_APP_URL to the CloudFront domain (WebAuthn RP is checksops.com).
```

Cognito WebAuthn RP ID must match the production pool (`checksops.com` if that is the canonical host). Staging passkeys do not transfer.

Plaid is not required. Leave Plaid disabled on the API.
